{"skill":{"slug":"kokoro-tts","displayName":"Kokoro TTS"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1769905003380,"changelog":"kokoro-tts 0.1.0\n\n- Initial release of the Kokoro TTS skill for generating speech audio from text.\n- Supports configuration via the KOKORO_API_URL environment variable.\n- Includes a Node.js script for generating audio files with customizable voice and speed.\n- Outputs MP3 file paths in a format compatible with OpenClaw for automatic audio attachment.\n- Provides several built-in voice options and instructions for listing all available voices.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"scripts/tts.js","size":1666,"sha256":"1c153ddfcd334d0c59de478c90bd584e7a626f02cc7dd1e70e50f873ab49e4c3","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"references/voices.md","size":488,"sha256":"a1d1d74f28a2307eb00a938f8182c64bbf3434a19403282aa91bfa8e661ace58","contentType":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1543,"sha256":"79fac3c48e8008b9ab69338da7d3827931ef1a5cd32d31e8cf0940988fb9a711","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1913,"sha256":"29e6a791c91fb3af6ec53feb209a77805e138f0b084e8f11957a4212eb310f28","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789027098629,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"d8a2c52f41261db40bf0d0883854a9cb6a6852b590a383d3ad4fb045fe7374c4","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/d8a2c52f41261db40bf0d0883854a9cb6a6852b590a383d3ad4fb045fe7374c4","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: kokoro-tts\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe skill is designed to generate speech using a configurable Kokoro TTS API. It makes a network POST request to the API_URL (defaulting to localhost) with user-provided text, voice, and speed, then saves the resulting audio to a local 'media' directory. There is no evidence of prompt injection in SKILL.md, malicious execution (user input is JSON-encoded, not executed), data exfiltration beyond sending the requested text to the configured TTS endpoint, or persistence mechanisms. All file and network operations are directly aligned with the stated purpose of a text-to-speech skill.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160574480},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":63,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":8,"checkedAt":1789027098629},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward text-to-speech helper that sends user-provided text to a configured Kokoro API and saves the resulting audio file.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The script reads KOKORO_API_URL and posts the supplied text to that endpoint, defaulting to localhost; remote endpoints are documented but users should understand that spoken text can leave the machine if configured that way.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No install script, dependency installation, hidden bootstrap, or remote code retrieval was found in the inspected artifacts.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The activation wording around asking to \"say\" something is somewhat broad, but the usage instructions are otherwise limited to explicit text-to-speech generation.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The only persistent effect observed is creating a media directory if needed and saving a generated MP3 file there; there are no services, scheduled tasks, credential access, privilege escalation, or cross-session hooks.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The behavior matches the stated TTS purpose: it takes text, voice, and speed arguments, calls a Kokoro speech endpoint, and writes an MP3 output. The frontmatter emphasizes a local engine, while the body also discloses local or remote API use.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you trust the Kokoro API endpoint configured in KOKORO_API_URL. Keep the default localhost endpoint for private text, and avoid speaking secrets or sensitive personal content through a remote server unless you trust that server.","findings":"[LP3] expected: Network access and environment configuration are expected for a configurable TTS API client, though a more explicit permission boundary would improve reviewability.\n[SQP-1] expected: The broad trigger language is a scoping weakness, but it points to speech generation rather than unrelated agent behavior.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending raw text to the configured TTS API and writing an MP3 are expected for this skill; the privacy implication should be made clearer for remote endpoint use.\n[SDI-1] expected: The local-only wording in the short description is partially inconsistent with the documented local-or-remote configuration, but the remote option is disclosed in the skill body.\n[SDI-2] expected: KOKORO_API_URL can point to an arbitrary endpoint, but this is user/environment-configured API routing for the TTS purpose rather than hidden exfiltration in the artifact.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789027098629}}}}}